## 12. Test Vectors (Normative, Reproducible)

Each vector specifies inputs and expected `(verdict, canonical_block_code, blocks_subset, allow_qualifiers)`. All vectors assume policy `2.0.0`, `paper` mode, single account `A1`, symbol BTCUSDT, default policy from §3 unless overridden.

### Vector TV-01 — Happy path open
- Inputs: action=open, side=buy, qty_base=0.01, limit_price=60000, price_ref=60000, leverage=3, margin=isolated, confidence=0.78, ev_bps=12, sl=59400, ttl_ms=1500, age=200ms
- Expected: `ALLOW`, blocks=[], qualifiers={}

### Vector TV-02 — Schema missing sl on open with require_sl_for_open=true
- Inputs: as TV-01 but bracket.sl_price=null
- Expected: `BLOCK`, canonical=`BLOCK:SL_MISSING`, blocks ⊇ [G17]

### Vector TV-03 — Multiple failures, precedence test
- Inputs: as TV-01 but mode=live, leverage=99, qty_base=10_000, sl=null
- Expected: `BLOCK`, canonical=`BLOCK:MODE_LIVE_DISABLED` (G1 wins by order), blocks ⊇ [G1, G14, G16, G17]
- Proves PREC-2 (lowest-ordered hard gate is canonical, all failures still listed).

### Vector TV-04 — Kill overrides approval
- Setup: global_kill.enabled=true, dangerous toggle live_enabled=true, valid approval row present
- Inputs: any valid live proposal
- Expected: `BLOCK`, canonical=`BLOCK:KILL` (G2)
- Proves PREC-3.

### Vector TV-05 — Approval pending HOLD
- Setup: live_enabled=true requested, approval row state=`pending`
- Inputs: valid proposal, mode=live
- Expected: `HOLD`, hold_reason=`awaiting_human_approval`, blocks ⊇ [G3]
- Proves PREC-1 HOLD conditions.

### Vector TV-06 — Idempotent retry
- Step 1: TV-01 → decision D1, ALLOW
- Step 2: same intent_id, new proposal_id, identical otherwise
- Expected: ALLOW, `duplicate_of=D1`, no counter delta, no dedupe insert
- Proves IDEM-1 to IDEM-3.

### Vector TV-07 — Proposal replay bug
- Step 1: TV-01 → D1
- Step 2: same proposal_id resubmitted
- Expected: `BLOCK`, canonical=`BLOCK:PROPOSAL_REPLAY`

### Vector TV-08 — Race duplicate (twin orchestrator paths)
- Step 1: TV-01 with intent_id=I1 → ALLOW
- Step 2: identical fingerprint with intent_id=I2 within 400ms
- Expected: `BLOCK`, canonical=`BLOCK:DUPLICATE_GUARD`, evidence.prior_decision_id=D1

### Vector TV-09 — Race duplicate after BLOCK does not poison
- Step 1: TV-02 (BLOCK:SL_MISSING) at t=0
- Step 2: TV-01 (valid) at t=100ms, same fingerprint, different intent_id
- Expected: Step 2 ALLOW (BLOCK did not insert into dedupe set)
- Proves DUP-INV-2.

### Vector TV-10 — Same intent, mutated qty
- Step 1: TV-01 (qty=0.01) ALLOW
- Step 2: same intent_id, new proposal_id, qty=0.02
- Expected: cache miss (different idempotency_key), G8 evaluates fresh → ALLOW (different fingerprint)
- Proves §6 + DUP-INV-1 boundary.

### Vector TV-11 — Stale price
- Inputs: TV-01 with price_ref_ts older than `max_price_ref_age_ms`
- Expected: `BLOCK`, canonical=`BLOCK:STALE_PRICE` (G5)

### Vector TV-12 — Stale features
- Inputs: TV-01 with feature_snapshot age > max
- Expected: `BLOCK`, canonical=`BLOCK:STALE_FEATURES` (G6)

### Vector TV-13 — Proposal TTL exceeded
- Inputs: TV-01 with created_at 6000ms ago, ttl_ms=1500
- Expected: `BLOCK`, canonical=`BLOCK:PROPOSAL_EXPIRED` (G7)

### Vector TV-14 — Rate limit
- Setup: emit 21 proposals/sec when cap=20
- Expected: 21st → `BLOCK:RATE_LIMIT` (G9), cool_down_ms applied

### Vector TV-15 — Confidence below min
- Inputs: TV-01 with confidence=0.30, min_open=0.55
- Expected: `BLOCK:CONFIDENCE_BELOW_MIN` (G10)

### Vector TV-16 — EV soft in paper, hard in live
- Inputs: TV-01 paper with ev_bps=-5
- Expected: ALLOW with `allow_qualifiers.applied_overrides=["G11_soft_warn"]`
- Same proposal under live policy → `BLOCK:EV_BELOW_MIN`

### Vector TV-17 — Order type not allowed
- Inputs: TV-01 with order_type=`stop_limit` while symbol overrides allow only `[market,limit]`
- Expected: `BLOCK:ORDER_TYPE_FORBIDDEN` (G12)

### Vector TV-18 — Cross margin without approval
- Inputs: margin_mode=cross, `dangerous_toggles.allow_cross_margin=false`
- Expected: `BLOCK:MARGIN_MODE_FORBIDDEN` (G13) AND `BLOCK:DANGEROUS_TOGGLE_NOT_APPROVED` (G27); canonical=G13

### Vector TV-19 — Leverage exceeded
- Inputs: leverage=20, BTCUSDT override max=5
- Expected: `BLOCK:LEVERAGE_EXCEEDED` (G14)

### Vector TV-20 — Price band violation
- Inputs: limit_price=63000 with price_ref=60000, band_bps=50
- Expected: `BLOCK:PRICE_BAND_VIOLATION` (G15)

### Vector TV-21 — Qty out of bounds
- Inputs: qty_base=0.00001, min_qty_base=0.001
- Expected: `BLOCK:QTY_OUT_OF_BOUNDS` (G16)

### Vector TV-22 — Liquidation proximity
- Setup: simulated liq distance 5bps, min required 50bps
- Expected: `BLOCK:LIQUIDATION_PROXIMITY` (G18)

### Vector TV-23 — Gross notional cap
- Setup: existing exposure 95k, cap 100k, new notional 10k
- Expected: `BLOCK:GROSS_NOTIONAL_CAP` (G19)

### Vector TV-24 — Daily loss limit reached
- Setup: realized_daily_loss = cap
- Expected: `BLOCK:DAILY_LOSS_LIMIT` (G24)

### Vector TV-25 — Drawdown halt
- Setup: equity drawdown_pct > max_drawdown_halt_pct
- Expected: `BLOCK:DRAWDOWN_HALT` (G26)

### Vector TV-26 — Soft cap transform
- Inputs: qty_base=1.2, symbol max=1.0, soft-cap enabled
- Expected: `ALLOW`, `capped_qty_base=1.0`, `applied_overrides=["G28_qty_cap"]`
- Proves PREC-5: transforms never upgrade BLOCK to ALLOW (here precondition was ALLOW).

### Vector TV-27 — Determinism
- Run TV-01 twice with frozen counter snapshot and same policy_hash
- Expected: byte-identical decision modulo `decision_id`, `decided_at`, `latency_ms`

### Vector TV-28 — Policy hot-reload mid-flight
- Setup: evaluation starts under policy_hash=H1; reload to H2 during eval
- Expected: decision carries `policy_hash=H1`; next proposal uses H2

### Vector TV-29 — Lock contention
- Setup: per-account lock held 60ms (>50ms timeout)
- Expected: `BLOCK:RATE_LIMIT` with reason `lock_contention`

### Vector TV-30 — Mode unknown
- Inputs: mode=`shadow` (not in enum)
- Expected: `BLOCK:SCHEMA` at G0 (enum violation), no further gates reported as failures

